      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Multicomponent MoS2/Co9S8/C hollow nanocubes were developed by the one-pot solvothermal method and a subsequent calcination process. Benefitting from the merits of hollow structures, the highly-conductive carbon matrix and the buffering effect provided by uniformly-mixed MoS2 and Co9S8, the MoS2/Co9S8/C anode shows high capacity and rate capability as the anode of sodium-ion batteries."},
